      "writtenOn": "2023-08-16T15:01:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since they all extend Texture, and that\u0027s meant to be threadsafe, it feels a little odd to say that the Dawn/VK portion are not threadsafe. Maybe it\u0027s not worth a lot of fuss if the eventual BackendTextureView object would change how these views are cached?\n\nI think a lock would be safest, and we can always go back to a single-threaded use case if we see it showing up in a bottleneck. If actual usage is mostly single-threaded, the locks should be pretty free since there won\u0027t be any contention.\n\nCC\u0027ing Greg to see if he has any thoughts.",
